title: Report back when candidate is rejected.
doc:
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |
    When the backing subsystem rejects a candidate during pre-validation checks
    (PVD hash mismatch or descriptor version acceptance failure), it now sends
    `CollatorProtocolMessage::Invalid` back to the collator protocol so the
    collator's reputation is penalized. Previously these cases silently dropped
    the candidate with no feedback.
crates:
- name: polkadot-node-core-backing
  bump: patch
